{
  "name": "174. Warp chat names a model call governance refused (warp-refusal) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "Warp's model calls are governed as whoever asked: the chat handler settles a grant from the dashboard request, including a virtual key sent in x-bf-vk. When governance refused that call - no access configured for the caller, an exhausted budget, a blocked model - Warp reported it as upstream_error, the code it uses for a provider outage, so the dashboard said Warp's model could not be reached and pointed the reader at the provider key. A signed-in user with no model access was told a credential had been revoked. Governance refusals now carry their own code, access_denied, and the no-access case says what to ask an administrator for while keeping governance's own reason. The case sends one chat with a virtual key that does not exist, which governance refuses before any provider is called, so no model tokens are spent. Red before the change: error.code was upstream_error. Every other governance refusal then shared access_denied too, so a spent budget was headlined to the user as having no access to Warp's model; each kind now has its own code (budget_exceeded, rate_limited, model_blocked). A second chat uses a run-scoped virtual key that allows only gpt-4o while Warp runs on gpt-4o-mini, which governance refuses as a blocked model before any provider is called, and expects model_blocked. Red before that change: error.code was access_denied. Requires the warp flag to be unlocked and the governance plugin enabled; the flag and the previous Warp config are restored at the end.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "openai warp-refusal setup: read warp feature flag",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Set again only by a read that really returned the flag (see the test script).",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('warpRefusalFlagWas');"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('warp-refusal: feature flags list', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.equal(200);",
              "});",
              "var flag;",
              "try { flag = (pm.response.json().flags || []).filter(function (f) { return f.id === 'warp'; })[0]; } catch (e) { flag = undefined; }",
              "pm.test('warp-refusal: warp flag exists', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(flag, 'no warp flag: ' + pm.response.text()).to.be.an('object');",
              "  pm.expect(flag.enabled, 'warp flag has no enabled state: ' + pm.response.text()).to.be.a('boolean');",
              "});",
              "// A failed read or a missing entry is not a disabled flag: record nothing, so the",
              "// enable and restore requests skip instead of switching off a flag that was on.",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200 && flag && typeof flag.enabled === 'boolean') {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('warpRefusalFlagWas', flag.enabled ? 'true' : 'false');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/feature-flags"
      }
    },
